{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And as for the Tabernacle, you shall make ten curtains.</b> In this He alluded to the ten utterances by which the world was created, to say that the Tabernacle is equivalent to the entire world, which was created by ten utterances; and it is also a merit for Israel through it, as if they had fulfilled the ten utterances by which the world was created." "Further, He intended in the order of this commandment — of the linen curtains and of the goats' hair curtains — that for the linen ones He commanded ten, and for the goats' hair ones He commanded eleven. He further commanded that one join five curtains separately and five curtains separately, and likewise for the goats' hair ones He commanded to join six separately. The reason for the matter is that HaShem inscribed His glorious Name in the curtains, and commanded that all of them have a width of four — whether of linen or of goats' hair — corresponding to the four letters of the Name הוי״ה. And so you will find that the earlier ones alluded in their pure statement (Shabbat 6a): 'private domain, its width four and its height ten' — which is after the Name הוי״ה: its width four and its height, meaning by the spelling-out of ten, on this pattern: יו״ד ה״י וא״ו ה״י. And He sanctified the inner one, because of its being close to the holy place, and commanded to make ten curtains corresponding to the letter יו״ד of His great Name, and commanded that one join five separately to allude thereby to the first letter ה״א of His Name, blessed be He. And He alluded in this that the first letter ה״א is always included within the letter יו״ד, and this is the sod of its pronunciation, for when you pronounce יו״ד you join וא״ו and דל״ת, which are the form of the ה״א on this pattern — ה׳ — and you pronounce only one letter; so too is this matter, and understand. And this dimension is the sod of חָכְמָה (wisdom), and behold, its inscription is visible in these curtains: חכמה — the first two letters are twenty-eight, corresponding to which He commanded the length of the curtain to be twenty-eight cubits. The third letter מ׳ — forty; corresponding to these HaShem commanded the width of four cubits, which for the count of ten curtains comes to forty. And the fourth letter is the letter ה׳, which He inscribed in the statement 'five separately,' and it is also the sod of the five acts of loving-kindness (חֲסָדִים) drawn from חָכְמָה. And afterwards HaShem commanded, corresponding to the completion of the Name, which is ו״ה, to make goats' hair curtains eleven, and inscribed that one join six separately — which corresponds to וא״ו — and five separately corresponding to ה״א; behold, the completion of His Name, blessed be He. He also inscribed in the calculation of the width — eleven, totaling forty-four (מ״ד) — for the sod of the וא״ו, the tiferet of Israel, which is the sod of יו״ד ה״א וא״ו ה״א, which totals מ״ה. And HaShem already informed us (Genesis 48:5) that one missing [from a] count will not prevent, for the totality completes it. And He inscribed in the calculation of the length — thirty cubits — corresponding to the gradations of the final ה״א in the Name, which shines from three [letters] that include [each] ten-tiers, and they are thirty. And yet there are supernal holy words belonging to Elohim, and he who has ears to hear will hear, and his heart will understand."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:33:47.217672643Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}